body:
We have quite a few places in our code where we do something like

``` python
@pytest.mark.requires_backend_interface(interface=RSABackend)
@pytest.mark.requires_backend_interface(interface=X509Backend)
```

Unfortunately it looks like this doesn't actually work (or rather, the class decorator doesn't work if there's more than one method in the class?). Additionally, even if it did work we do this:

``` python
    if "backend" in metafunc.fixturenames:
        filtered_backends = []
        required = metafunc.function.requires_backend_interface
        required_interfaces = tuple(
            mark.kwargs["interface"] for mark in required
        )
        for backend in selected_backends:
            if isinstance(backend, required_interfaces):
                filtered_backends.append(backend)
```

`isinstance` will return True if any of the interfaces are available. We need to require all of them with something more like (warning: sleep deprived code)

``` python
        for backend in selected_backends:
            all_interfaces = True
            for req_int in required_interfaces:
                if not isinstance(backend, req_int):
                    all_interfaces = False

            if all_interfaces:
                filtered_backends.append(backend)
```

We should figure out the pytest bug (if any) so we can submit a patch upstream and also correct our filtering code.
